From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x-j72: Wake on the D2089 source
 event

A live unplug/replug cycle on the iPad Air (Cellular) latched D2089 event
0 at the replug edge.  This is also the event identified as the D2089 plug
event from iOS 12 when support for this PMIC was added.

Give that event to the charger after its line and ADC interrupts.  The
charger can then arm the real PMIC event as a wake source instead of
relying on polling while the system is asleep.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
@@ -11,4 +11,10 @@
 / {
 	compatible = "apple,j72", "apple,s5l8960x", "apple,arm-platform";
 	model = "Apple iPad Air (Cellular)";
 };
+
+&tristar_charger {
+	interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+		     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+		     <0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+};
-- 
